    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9wy3a6x",
      "content": "1. GDP measures final goods and services produced within domestic territory."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lu4z824",
      "content": "2. GNP equals GDP plus Net Factor Income from Abroad."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nyd0fjf",
      "content": "3. NDP equals GDP minus depreciation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "37vasty",
      "content": "4. NNP at factor cost is called National Income."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t6clm7i",
      "content": "5. Real GDP is measured at constant prices."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "at7m1di",
      "content": "6. Nominal GDP is measured at current prices."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rd26qpr",
      "content": "7. GVA equals GDP minus Net Indirect Taxes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7558top",
      "content": "8. Per capita income equals national income divided by population."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mn7cgxq",
      "content": "9. Base year for India’s GDP is 2011–12."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xwrs43o",
      "content": "10. Primary sector includes agriculture and allied activities."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9nfduz6",
      "content": "11. Secondary sector includes manufacturing and industry."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qhow1mz",
      "content": "12. Tertiary sector includes services."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p0bwan8",
      "content": "13. Mixed economy has both public and private sectors."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lb1cbjk",
      "content": "14. Depreciation is also called consumption of fixed capital."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xa8cnc3",
      "content": "15. Factor cost excludes indirect taxes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ligtu7e",
      "content": "16. Market price includes indirect taxes and subsidies."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i9nvptd",
      "content": "17. Disposable income equals personal income minus direct taxes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7lfsj2o",
      "content": "18. Personal income includes transfer payments."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0otktlr",
      "content": "19. Transfer payments do not add to GDP."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cmi8g5m",
      "content": "20. Intermediate goods are excluded from GDP calculation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tlwcyt4",
      "content": "21. Final goods are included in GDP."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o718uhb",
      "content": "22. Double counting is avoided in GDP calculation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9ixtxkp",
      "content": "23. Value added method avoids double counting."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e770xqr",
      "content": "24. Income method sums factor incomes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sdm9bc1",
      "content": "25. Expenditure method sums consumption, investment, government spending and net exports."
    },
    {
      "id": "cowro6x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j4vj65o",
      "content": "26. CPI measures retail inflation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yt0ves7",
      "content": "27. WPI measures wholesale inflation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sctob62",
      "content": "28. Core inflation excludes food and fuel."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ridand5",
      "content": "29. Headline inflation includes all commodities."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qe8mxj8",
      "content": "30. Demand-pull inflation arises from excess demand."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ez3jtvw",
      "content": "31. Cost-push inflation arises from increased production costs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "16i4hy6",
      "content": "32. Hyperinflation is extremely rapid inflation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nodvppn",
      "content": "33. Stagflation combines inflation and unemployment."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ok8741c",
      "content": "34. Deflation is a sustained fall in price level."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "efiggmh",
      "content": "35. Disinflation is a fall in inflation rate."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zye0w0p",
      "content": "36. CPI is used for inflation targeting in India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sa1cygq",
      "content": "37. Inflation targeting framework adopted in 2016."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "on7hrzt",
      "content": "38. Target inflation rate in India is 4% ± 2%."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o5hdpia",
      "content": "39. Imported inflation occurs due to rise in global prices."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "toqksiw",
      "content": "40. Wage-price spiral fuels inflation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9l1uohg",
      "content": "41. Supply shocks can trigger inflation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yw6gvov",
      "content": "42. Phillips Curve shows inverse relation between inflation and unemployment."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "td5u630",
      "content": "43. Core CPI excludes volatile components."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ogikz9g",
      "content": "44. Food inflation significantly impacts CPI."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o8mqwx0",
      "content": "45. Inflation reduces purchasing power."
    },
    {
      "id": "5ebpa4w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "BANKING & RBI"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3vixgnm",
      "content": "46. RBI was established in 1935."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y68qn4n",
      "content": "47. RBI was nationalised in 1949."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9jh67cb",
      "content": "48. Repo rate is the main policy rate of RBI."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Monetary policy aims to maintain price stability while keeping in mind the objective of growth.",
      "id": "zcfm9a0"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dl5sds9",
      "content": "49. Reverse repo rate absorbs excess liquidity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6orcxon",
      "content": "50. CRR is cash reserve maintained with RBI."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ljx4r2w",
      "content": "51. SLR is liquid asset reserve maintained by banks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zzkxn8g",
      "content": "52. MSF is emergency borrowing facility."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3tceux4",
      "content": "53. LAF stands for Liquidity Adjustment Facility."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "08orh89",
      "content": "54. Open Market Operations regulate liquidity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z9shgqt",
      "content": "55. Bank rate is long-term lending rate."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3lbpeyk",
      "content": "56. NBFCs are regulated by RBI."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0l2re0e",
      "content": "57. NPA is loan overdue for more than 90 days."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uzze7rl",
      "content": "58. Basel norms relate to capital adequacy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "enj6nbd",
      "content": "59. Capital Adequacy Ratio ensures bank stability."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8pxisg0",
      "content": "60. MCLR is benchmark lending rate."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zm3tfah",
      "content": "61. Priority Sector Lending supports agriculture and MSMEs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ve2zwaj",
      "content": "62. Digital payments reduce cash dependence."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a5g4gvc",
      "content": "63. UPI is real-time payment system."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rpnccs8",
      "content": "64. Financial inclusion expands banking access."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bhxxfzk",
      "content": "65. RBI issues currency notes except ₹1 note."
    },
    {
      "id": "8jt0254",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "FISCAL POLICY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xao1feu",
      "content": "66. Fiscal deficit indicates total borrowing requirement."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "86qnevj",
      "content": "67. Revenue deficit indicates excess revenue expenditure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zbin8zl",
      "content": "68. Primary deficit excludes interest payments."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nbq3q8h",
      "content": "69. FRBM Act enacted in 2003."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kou4b5d",
      "content": "70. GST implemented on 1 July 2017."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zy5n9gz",
      "content": "71. GST is destination-based tax."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y8pglw7",
      "content": "72. CGST and SGST apply to intra-state supply."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "94c4srg",
      "content": "73. IGST applies to inter-state supply."
    },
